<%#
  T-28 — the page a share link answers with when it will not serve.

  --- WHY THIS PAGE IS DELIBERATELY BARE ---

  Its reader is very often NOT a Redmine user: a public link (FR-62) is opened by whoever
  was sent it, on an instance they have no account on and whose navigation means nothing to
  them. So there is one sentence, and it is the whole page. No project, no template name, no
  "who to ask" — every one of those would tell a stranger something about an installation
  they have no relationship with, and the refusal is not made more useful by any of them.

  It renders inside Redmine's `base` layout rather than a layout of this plugin's, because
  §9b's rule is native chrome and because a page that looks like the rest of the instance is
  what tells a reader the link reached the right place and simply is not live any more.
%>
<h2><%= l(:label_reporter_share_refused) %></h2>

<p class="nodata"><%= @message %></p>
